          dealing: 'Each player receives 9 cards. 13 cards form a talon (Pila).',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Win more tricks than either of the other two players individually.',
          gameplay: "1. Must follow suit if possible.\n2. Highest Matador wins any trick, followed by other trumps, then high cards of led suit.\n3. **Puesta**: If the Hombre doesn't win more tricks than one opponent, they 'lose' and must pay the pot.",
          keyRules: [
            'Must follow suit if possible; if void, may play any card.',
            'In game contracts, Spadille (A of spades) and Basta (A of clubs) are permanent trumps; Manille is second highest (2 in black trumps, 7 in red).',
            'Matadors have limited follow-suit exemptions: when a trump is led, you need not play a matador unless a higher matador was led and you have no other trumps.',
            'Declarer wins by taking more tricks than either defender; nolo contracts: declarer must take no tricks.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Prioritize the Spadille. If you hold the Ace of Spades, you have a 90% chance of winning your first lead. Use it to 'flush' the opponents' trumps early.",
          intermediate: "Hand Evaluation: Only bid 'Solo' if you hold at least two of the three top Matadors and four other trumps. In a 3-player game, card density is high, so a single missing Matador can be fatal.",
          advanced: 'The Defensive Pinch: As the two defenders against the Hombre, you must cooperate. If you have the lead and know your partner has no trumps left, lead a suit where the Hombre is likely weak to force them to use a high Matador early.',
          tips: [
            "Remember the 'Manille' changes depending on the trump suit! In Diamonds, it is the 2; in Spades, it is the 7.",
            'If the Hombre takes cards from the Talon, watch which cards they discard. It tells you exactly which suits they are void in.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
